<title>ITALY: Europaams gets go-head to award missile contracts.</title>
<headline>Europaams gets go-head to award missile contracts.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-05-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Ministries of Defence of Italy, France and Britain on Monday gave the go-ahead for the awarding of contracts for the development and initial production of the new missile system Paams being developed by the three nations.</p>
<p>The new Italian-French-British missile system is being developed for the future self defence and air defence of frigates in the navies of the three nations.</p>
<p>This was announced in a statement from the consortium Eurosam, which has a 66 percent stake in the joint venture Europaams -- which is developing the Paams missile system -- while Ukams has a 33 percent stake.</p>
<p>Italy's Alenia Difesa, part of the state-controlled Finmeccanica holds 50 percent of the Eurosam consortium with French groups Aerospatiale having 25 percent and Thomson-CSF 25 percent.</p>
<p>British Aerospace, GEC-Marconi and Siemens Plessey Electronic Systems each have a 33 percent stake in Ukams.</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129502</p>
</text>
